# Gridlock Traffic Demand Prediction

## Overview

This project aims to predict traffic demand using machine learning models trained on spatio-temporal traffic data. The solution focuses on extensive feature engineering, gradient boosting models, ensembling, and stacking techniques to maximize predictive performance.

The final solution uses:

- LightGBM
- CatBoost
- XGBoost
- Weighted Ensembling
- Stacking (Ridge Regression Meta Model)

---

## Problem Statement

Traffic congestion is a major challenge in modern cities. Accurate traffic demand prediction helps transportation authorities and city planners optimize traffic flow, reduce congestion, and improve infrastructure planning.

The objective is to predict traffic demand for unseen observations using historical traffic and environmental data.

